{"meta":{"format_version":"4.5","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"fairy","model_identifier":"fairy","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"FAIRY (fairy.bbmodel)  -  notes\n==================================================================\nNew commission for Survive and Conquer: flying female fairy, blue skin, big yellow eyes, long blonde\nhair, two blue antennae, short white dress, silver crown with gem, silver wand with star tip,\nmonarch-layout butterfly wings painted white/yellow with thin black veins & edges.\nScale 1 unit = 2.8125 cm. Faces -Z (Blockbench north), creature right = +X.\nFormat: Blockbench 4.5, model_format \"free\" (Generic), per-face UV, nearest filtering.\nTexture: ONE embedded atlas fairy.png 512x512 (resolution == uv_width/uv_height == image size, so every\n  face maps the same way in any Blockbench version / loader).\n  - body & props: top-left 128x64 area at 1 texel/unit, fully opaque (opaque backing everywhere else too).\n  - wings: right half at 8 texels/unit: forewing art 230x267 at texel (256,0), hindwing art 170x182 at (256,280).\n  ALPHA IS USED (wings only): binary alpha, transparent texels are exactly 0 and their RGB is padded with\n  the neighbouring edge colour, so filtering/mipmaps cannot bleed a fringe.  GAME MATERIAL MUST USE\n  alphaTest (~0.5) (or transparent+depthWrite with alphaTest); otherwise the wing planes show as rectangles.\n  Blockbench textured view renders the cut-outs; Blockbench's untextured \"Solid\" view mode shows the plain\n  wing rectangles (expected for any alpha cut-out).\n\nORIGIN / HOVER CHOICE\n  root pivot = (0,0,0) ON THE GROUND (selection ring / shadow / hit box base stay at y=0).\n  Geometry lift: every cube and pivot is raised by 3.9264 u (0.11 m) so that in idle the\n  LOW point of the bob has soles / toes touching y\u22480, and the HIGH point is only a small hop above that.\n  Bob amplitude and timing are unchanged; the whole hover+bob was translated down. In-game elevation\n  (how high she flies) is applied by game code, not baked into the model.\n  No extra bone was inserted: baseline chain root > hips > torso > head kept; bob is a hips position key.\n  Death still falls face-down and holds with the lowest body point on y=0.\n\nSIZE\n  Cubes: 73  (all axis-aligned; 0 rotated cubes). See CUBE BUDGET below.\n  Body height (sole -> head top, standing frame): 57.0 u = 1.60 m (brief: female 1.60 m = 57 u).\n  Default pose: soles y=3.9, head top y=60.9, hair top y=61.9, crown top y=67.18, antenna bulbs top y=71.2.\n  Wing top (default/flat-spread pose): y=77.1 = 16.2 u above head top.\n  Wing top during idle: y=75.7..78.9 (always above the crown at 67.2).\n  Wingspan (flat): 62.0 u = 1.74 m.  Wing face area (both sides) 1777 u^2 ~ 2.8x the body front silhouette (~640 u^2).\n  Idle lowest point (toes) y=0.3..3.1  -> she hovers ~1 cm off the ground.\n\nHIT BOX (W x H x D, units, base on ground, centred x=0,z=0)\n  Body (low-bob on ground to crown): 16 x 67 x 12  (= 0.45 x 1.89 x 0.34 m)\n  Optional wing box (selection/click only): 62 x 43 x 14 starting at y=36.\n\nMOVE SPEEDS (in-place cycles; flight, so no foot sliding to match)\n  walk (= fly): designed 1.5 m/s = 53.3 u/s, cycle 1.250 s (3 wing strokes)\n  run  (fast fly): designed 3.0 m/s = 106.7 u/s, cycle 1.000 s (3 wing strokes)\n\nCLIPS (name, length, loop mode, events)\n  idle           2.000 s  loop \n      hover; 4 strokes x 0.50 s; body rises on each downstroke (wings sweep from back to spread) and dips on the upstroke; hair/antennae/skirt/legs follow-through; seamless\n  walk           1.250 s  loop \n      forward flight hover: lean fwd, stronger/faster strokes, bob synced, legs trail, hair streams back\n  run            1.000 s  loop \n      fast flight: deeper lean, fastest/strongest strokes, hair & antennae swept back\n  attack_spell   1.250 s  once   KEY = 0.5833 s (frame 14 @24fps)\n      one-handed wand cast: anticipation, wand raised beside head, thrust/flick forward; left arm reaches forward on wind-up then pulls down/out as counterbalance (FK only); big wing wind-up and power stroke whose full spread lands exactly on KEY\n  injured        0.500 s  once \n      hit from front: jolt back/down, head snaps, arms flinch up, legs kick, wings snap shut then resume; back to idle pose (same stroke phase) at the end\n  death          2.200 s  hold   land = 1.00 s\n      hit, weak flutter, wings close straight back, falls face-down (gravity drop) while rotating, lands ~1.00 s with a small bounce, wings flop open and drape; holds last frame on y=0\n  attack_spell wand-tip (slot_wand_tip / glow_wand_star centre) WORLD position at KEY:\n      (-0.8, 51.8, -33.3) units  = (-0.02, 1.46, -0.94) m relative to the model origin (spawn the bolt here, aimed at the target).\n  KEY / land times are also stored as Blockbench animation markers.\n  Root bone only moves in death (lands with lowest body point at y=0.00).\n\nATTACHMENT POINTS (empty groups; pivot = attach point in default pose)\n  slot_head        parent head         pivot (0.00, 60.93, 0.00)\n  slot_back        parent torso        pivot (0.00, 42.93, 3.50)\n  slot_quiver      parent torso        pivot (2.50, 45.93, 3.50)\n  slot_shoulder_r  parent torso        pivot (4.50, 49.93, 0.00)\n  slot_carry       parent torso        pivot (0.00, 40.93, -4.50)\n  slot_hand_r      parent hand_r       pivot (6.25, 31.43, 0.00)\n  slot_wand_tip    parent wand         pivot (6.25, 31.43, -13.50)\n  slot_shield_l    parent arm_lower_l  pivot (-9.00, 36.93, 0.00)\n  slot_hand_l      parent hand_l       pivot (-6.25, 31.43, 0.00)\n  slot_hip_r       parent hips         pivot (5.50, 32.93, 3.00)\n  slot_hip_l       parent hips         pivot (-5.50, 32.93, 3.00)\n  slot_wand_tip = spell spawn locator at the centre of the star (child of the wand bone).\n\nWAND (bone \"wand\" under slot_hand_r; pivot = grip = slot_hand_r pivot)\n  Slim silver shaft 0.8 u, butt cap behind the fist, collar, glow_wand_star core + 5 star points.\n  Brief convention: wand runs forward (-Z) when the arm hangs straight (default pose); wand bone rest 0.\n  In clips the forearm is raised so the wand stands up in front of her; the fist grip keeps the shaft\n  perpendicular to the forearm (it never passes through the arm; validator checks this every frame).\n  glow_wand_star is named for in-game glow; no particles/lights in the file.\n\nSKELETON\n  Baseline names kept: root > hips > torso > head (> slot_head); arm_upper/arm_lower/hand _r/_l;\n  leg_upper/leg_lower/foot _r/_l; all baseline slot_* points. Extra bones (secondary motion / props):\n  skirt (hips), hair_back_1 > hair_back_2 > hair_back_3, hair_lock_r/_l, antenna_r/_l (head),\n  wing_fore_r/_l, wing_hind_r/_l (torso, pivots at the wing roots), wand > slot_wand_tip.\n  Rest rotations: only antenna_r/_l carry a small outward/forward rest tilt; everything else rest 0.\n  Wings rest flat-spread in the XY plane (shows the pattern in Blockbench); clips sweep them about Y.\n  Forewing/hindwing are separate bones; hindwing trails the forewing by 7% of a stroke.\n\nWINGS\n  One thin plane cube per wing bone (4 total, 0.2 u thick): wing_fore_r/l_plane, wing_hind_r/l_plane.\n  Only north/south faces are textured (south = same art mirrored = underside); the 4 thin side faces have\n  no texture, so nothing outlines the transparent part of the plane.\n  Silhouette: smooth monarch outline cut by alpha - long arched costa, rounded-pointed apex, near-straight\n  termen, rounded tornus on the forewing; pear-shaped rounded hindwing.  Edge steps are 1/8 unit.\n  Venation (thin, 1 texel = 0.125 u; cell edges 1.5 texels): forewing Sc, closed discal cell with angled\n  discocellular cross-veins, R1 + R2 free, R3/R4/R5 on a common stalk to the apex, M1-M3, Cu1-Cu2, 2A;\n  hindwing humeral spur, Sc+R1, long closed discal cell, Rs, M1-M3, Cu1-Cu2, 2A, 3A.\n  Black outer margin band (~1.2-1.35 u) with two rows of small white / pale-yellow dots, rounded \"loop\"\n  cell ends where veins meet the band, thin black costa, dark forewing apex with sub-apical spots.\n  Colours unchanged in spirit: yellow cells (deep at the base, pale outward), white sub-apical cells.\n  Forewing/hindwing planes overlap a little at the forewing's inner edge (as on a real butterfly); with\n  the hindwing phase lag, that inner edge can graze the hindwing plane for a few frames (sub-unit, hidden).\n\nTEAM COLOUR\n  team_sash: thin waist ribbon in placeholder team blue RGB (52,96,178) for the game to tint. The blue\n  skin palette deliberately avoids that exact value (skin base 108,162,234) so a colour-key tint is safe.\n  If the fairy ends up neutral/hostile, re-texture the sash white.\n\nCUBE BUDGET\n  73 cubes. Brief cube budgets are soft guidance (Josh: extra detail is welcome).  Breakdown:\n  wings 4 planes (were 20 stepped cubes before the alpha wings), crown 10, wand+star 9, antennae 6, hair 11, rest of body/dress 33.\n  Cheap LOD if needed: drop crown points/side bands, star points, ears, nose, thumbs, bracelets (-18).\n\nCONVENTIONS / CAVEATS\n  - Rotation signs follow the reference files (Bedrock-style X/Y negation), verified by FK render.\n  - All keys sampled from smooth curves (24 fps; slow secondary bones 12 fps in loops), catmullrom,\n    unwrapped on the short arc: no Euler wraps, no limb flips (validator checks every frame).\n  - Loops: last key == first key; one-shots start/end in the idle t=0 pose and wing phase.\n  - Some soft overlap where wing roots enter the long hair is intentional (wings emerge from under the hair).\n  - Deliberate brief deviations, requested by Josh for the wings: 8 texels/unit (brief: 1 texel/unit) and a\n    512x512 atlas (brief lists 32-256).  Body/props still follow the 1 texel/unit pixel-art rule.\n"},"resolution":{"width":512,"height":512},"elements":[{"name":"waist","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-3.75,34.4264,-2.25],"to":[3.75,40.4264,2.25],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0.0,34.9264,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[108.0,36.0,116.0,42.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[116.0,36.0,120.0,42.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[120.0,36.0,128.0,42.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[104.0,36.0,108.0,42.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[108.0,32.0,116.0,36.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[116.0,32.0,124.0,36.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"c949ff39-4fd8-55d3-958d-a78b526e54fd"},{"name":"chest","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-4.5,39.9264,-2.75],"to":[4.5,50.4264,2.5],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0.0,34.9264,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[93.0,5.0,102.0,15.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[102.0,5.0,107.0,15.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[107.0,5.0,116.0,15.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[88.0,5.0,93.0,15.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[93.0,0.0,102.0,5.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[102.0,0.0,111.0,5.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"521f5f24-a61c-59c9-8c24-e41a61d9c997"},{"name":"bust","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-5.22,42.4014,-4.91],"to":[5.22,48.7014,-2.45],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0.0,45.5514,-2.75],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[62.0,45.0,71.0,50.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[71.0,45.0,73.0,50.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[73.0,45.0,82.0,50.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[60.0,45.0,62.0,50.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[62.0,43.0,71.0,45.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[71.0,43.0,80.0,45.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"11c2a362-2395-5b66-9398-d9f31b274298"},{"name":"bust_front","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-4.44,43.1214,-5.87],"to":[4.44,48.0414,-4.91],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0.0,45.5514,-2.75],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[17.0,54.0,24.0,58.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[24.0,54.0,25.0,58.0],"t